    <!-- The dictionary's tags: the part-of-speech, usage, kanji and kana,
         dialect, field and proper-noun type codes the dictionary
         declares, drawn as the Word tab's chips and the Forms tab's class
         heading. Named tag_<code>, with "-" in a code written as "_" and
         the case kept: iK and ik are different tags.
         The English started as the dictionary's own labels and is now the
         app's wording: a later rewording in the dictionary does not reach
         the UI unless this file is edited. The screens lowercase it.
         A code missing here shows the dictionary's own English label
         (see ui/labels/DictionaryLabels.kt), which is how a code a later
         dictionary adds still gets a chip. DictionaryLabelsTest holds
         this file and values-ja/tags.xml to the codes in pos-codes.tsv,
         both ways. -->
